A||N||2||DaveL||Slipperry Brake Sliders||||5||
Z||000000||DaveL||03-02-2000||10:34 AM||||Recently put new pads on the front of my 87 SE. Should the brake sleeves or "sliders" normally be removed and relubed during pad replacement? I never even took mine out, but now when I ride slowly I get a pronounced rattle in the front end which stops when any brake pressure is applied at all. If the O-rings were missing, either one or both on any caliper slider, would it cause rattling like that? Lastly, are replacements available at GM or aftermarket, for sliders? I'm pretty sure the O-rings and boots come in the caliper repair kits available abywhere, but not about the sliders.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Shiner||03-02-2000||10:46 AM||||DEFINATLY lube up the sliders before you put the brakes back on, or take them back off and lube if you already put they back on!!!  The calipers need to slide one these.  I need a couple new boots too, but I don't feel like blowing my hard earned money on a compleate caliper rebuild kit when they work fine other wise.  If you find a place to get JUST the slider boots, LMK||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||03-02-2000||07:18 PM||||rattle, if your sure it's brakes, means either the caliper is loose or you installed the pads wrong or your pads are missing hardware.||||reg||1
